# Always passes null for vx in release()'s flyOut call, including on a mouse
# release (docs/plans/2026-10-01-swipe-momentum.md, decision 2). Every mouse
# commit then falls back to the fixed SWIPE_OUT_MS/SWIPE_OUT_EASE curve, so a
# fast flick restarts the card from a standstill instead of continuing at the
# speed it was released - the replayed start speed sits at 0, not the live
# release speed this test measures.
# Re-cut 2026-10-03 (AP1-a): release() now executes releaseDecision() and both pointerdown sites call canStartGesture(); the mutation is re-expressed on the new site, intent unchanged.
